    "source": "Etruria Industrial Museum - geograph.org.uk - 2187647",
    "description": "Etruria Industrial Museum, near to Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent, Great Britain.\nJesse Shirley's Bone and Flint Mill between the Caldon and Trent &amp; Mersey Canals, Stoke on Trent (this small arm is on the T&amp;M). The low part of the building houses the boiler, to the left of it is the beam engine house. This then leads onto the mill, top floor is the pan room and bottom the gears. The 'chimney' on the end is a flint calciner/kiln. \n\nTo the upper right of the picture the Jesse Shirley's company is in modern premises still producing calcined bone ash to the potters.",
